DevOps Interview Preparation
2–4 Years Experience | Tool 13 Monitoring & Observability – Production Level Systems

For 2–4 years experience, interviewers expect you to design monitoring, create meaningful alerts, and troubleshoot production incidents — not just install tools.

🔹 Core Monitoring Concepts

• What is monitoring vs observability?
• Metrics vs logs vs traces
• White-box vs black-box monitoring
• SLIs, SLOs & SLAs — why they matter?
• Alert fatigue — how do you avoid it?
• What should you monitor in production systems?

🔹 Prometheus Interview Questions (2–4 yrs)

• Prometheus architecture
• Pull vs push model — pros & cons
• Types of Prometheus metrics
• Exporters and ServiceMonitor
• PromQL basics (interview-level)
• Recording rules — why are they needed?
• Alertmanager — how it works?
• Prometheus with Kubernetes
• Handling high-cardinality metrics
• Prometheus scaling strategies
• Securing Prometheus endpoints
🔹 Grafana Interview Questions

• Grafana vs Kibana
• Data sources in Grafana
• Dashboard & panel design best practices
• Variables and templating
• Grafana alerting
• Dashboard sharing & permissions
• Grafana provisioning

🔹 Cloud Monitoring (AWS / Azure / GCP)

• CloudWatch vs Azure Monitor vs Cloud Monitoring
• Logs, metrics & alerts in cloud
• Centralized logging architecture
• Monitoring cloud-native services
• Cost-aware monitoring

🔹 Real-World Monitoring Scenarios

• Alert triggered but application is healthy — why?
• Too many alerts during peak traffic — how to fix?
• Prometheus not scraping targets — troubleshooting steps
• Grafana dashboard showing no data — what will you check?
• CPU is normal but application is slow — next steps?

💡 Interview Tip:
If you say:
👉 “We monitor SLIs, use meaningful alerts, and troubleshoot using metrics + logs”
you already sound like a production-ready DevOps engineer.
